Reason:
The fix removes the forced addition of EXT4_GET_BLOCKS_CONVERT from the caller, so that the split is performed without the conversion flag. In ext4_split_convert_extents, the condition for splitting now includes both UNWRIT_EXT and CONVERT flags, but the split_flag only adds EXT4_EXT_DATA_VALID2 when the original flags include CONVERT (which is the case for fallocate zero range, not for pre-IO splitting). This ensures that when splitting before I/O, the on-disk extent remains unwritten, and only the extent status tree marks the split portion as unwritten (via MARK_UNWRIT2). The entire extent range is zeroed out for consistency, preventing stale data exposure if the I/O fails.

